# {{TITLE}}: principles

The rulebook behind the one-page list in `../SKILL.md`. Started {{DATE}}.
Sources are in `video-index.md`; per-video notes in `videos/<id>.md`.

How to read it:

- `(Creator m:ss)` is a source: who said it and where in their video.
- Numbers are the creators' own words. Anything worked out here rather than
  said in a video is marked **(inference)**.
- "History" says which video introduced a lesson (NEW), which backed it up
  (AGREES) and which disagreed (CONFLICTS, with how).
- If a lesson was only seen on screen and never said aloud, the source says
  so: `(Creator 2:10, on screen)`.

